{"title": "Show HN: Music player for visually exploring music collection", "link": "https://github.com/Cliff-Lee/melodex", "summary": "<p>I created Melodex for rediscovering my music collection. I got bored of listening to the same songs over and over. Shuffle didn't do it for me either, as I wanted something that moved between the songs like a journey with more cohesion.<p>Alongside the ability to plan routes from a starting song to a final destination, the routes through the music map are navigable too.<p>There's a few other features like plugins to connect radio stations, or other music sources too which were a big project in terms of getting the plugin structure right to get working with almost any online source now.<p>Looking for feedback on the music map, how it can be further improved, how intuitive, did it lead to new musical discoveries of your music?</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50228579\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50228579</a></p>\n<p>Points: 1</p>\n<p># Comments: 0</p>", "published": "2026-10-25T05:23:26+00:00", "source": "Hacker News Best", "category": "techblog", "matched_entities": {}, "ontology": {"repo": "BlogRadar", "category": "techblog", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "source_event_model": "blog_post", "event_model_id": "tech.blog_post", "evidence_policy_ids": ["source_metadata", "article_text"], "event_model_payload": {"headline": "Show HN: Music player for visually exploring music collection", "source_name": "Hacker News Best", "source_url": "https://github.com/Cliff-Lee/melodex", "published_at": "2026-10-25T05:23:26+00:00", "summary": "<p>I created Melodex for rediscovering my music collection. I got bored of listening to the same songs over and over. Shuffle didn't do it for me either, as I wanted something that moved between the songs like a journey with more cohesion.<p>Alongside the ability to plan routes from a starting song to a final destination, the routes through the music map are navigable too.<p>There's a few other features like plugins to connect radio stations, or other music sources too which were a big project in terms of getting the plugin structure right to get working with almost any online source now.<p>Looking for feedback on the music map, how it can be further improved, how intuitive, did it lead to new musical discoveries of your music?</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50228579\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50228579</a></p>\n<p>Points: 1</p>\n<p># Comments: 0</p>"}}, "logged_at": "2026-10-25T05:46:20.693839+00:00"}
