{"title": "Show HN: Independent Vet – Find locally owned vets (and corporate ones) near you", "link": "https://independentvet.com/", "summary": "<p>Three years ago, our dog was sideswiped by a car and my wife took him to the local vet in Berkeley. Unfortunately, things did not go well and to cut a long story short, he passed after 2 days and $13k of bills for very limited care. I was surprised to learn that the seemingly mom & pop practice had been acquired by a PE-owned consolidator and that around 50% of practices in the US are now owned by mostly PE-backed corporate groups - a trend that rapidly accelerated after COVID.<p>I started a small janky passion project called <a href=\"https://privateequityvet.org\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://privateequityvet.org</a> which used Leaflet.js to map corporately owned veterinary practices in the US. The site gradually took off, was covered on PBS Newshour and now gets 20k uniques a day.<p>A few months ago I launched IndependentVet.com which aims to be the opposite of the original site, helping pet parents in the US/Canada/UK identify locally owned veterinary practices. Just yesterday I launched native mobile apps that I developed over the course of three intense weeks of evenings and weekends using Opus 5.5. While it's early days, I'm really happy with how it turned out: <a href=\"https://independentvet.com/get\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://independentvet.com/get</a><p>Would love to hear what you think!</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50228314\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50228314</a></p>\n<p>Points: 2</p>\n<p># Comments: 0</p>", "published": "2026-10-25T04:26:00+00:00", "source": "Hacker News Best", "category": "techblog", "matched_entities": {}, "ontology": {"repo": "BlogRadar", "category": "techblog", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "source_event_model": "blog_post", "event_model_id": "tech.blog_post", "evidence_policy_ids": ["source_metadata", "article_text"], "event_model_payload": {"headline": "Show HN: Independent Vet – Find locally owned vets (and corporate ones) near you", "source_name": "Hacker News Best", "source_url": "https://independentvet.com/", "published_at": "2026-10-25T04:26:00+00:00", "summary": "<p>Three years ago, our dog was sideswiped by a car and my wife took him to the local vet in Berkeley. Unfortunately, things did not go well and to cut a long story short, he passed after 2 days and $13k of bills for very limited care. I was surprised to learn that the seemingly mom & pop practice had been acquired by a PE-owned consolidator and that around 50% of practices in the US are now owned by mostly PE-backed corporate groups - a trend that rapidly accelerated after COVID.<p>I started a small janky passion project called <a href=\"https://privateequityvet.org\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://privateequityvet.org</a> which used Leaflet.js to map corporately owned veterinary practices in the US. The site gradually took off, was covered on PBS Newshour and now gets 20k uniques a day.<p>A few months ago I launched IndependentVet.com which aims to be the opposite of the original site, helping pet parents in the US/Canada/UK identify locally owned veterinary practices. Just yesterday I launched native mobile apps that I developed over the course of three intense weeks of evenings and weekends using Opus 5.5. While it's early days, I'm really happy with how it turned out: <a href=\"https://independentvet.com/get\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://independentvet.com/get</a><p>Would love to hear what you think!</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50228314\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50228314</a></p>\n<p>Points: 2</p>\n<p># Comments: 0</p>"}}, "logged_at": "2026-10-25T05:46:20.693839+00:00"}
